course: dictionary
lesson: 10464
title: The tuba
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tuba is a very large brass instrument with a wide bell. You play it by blowing into a mouthpiece. «The tuba is the biggest and lowest brass instrument, and the trumpet is small and high.» So the tuba makes the deepest notes, and the trumpet makes higher ones.
explain: Brass means a family of instruments made of metal that you play by buzzing your lips into a mouthpiece. «Brass players buzz their lips into the mouthpiece; the trumpet, trombone, horn and tuba are brass.» The clue is in the list: these four are all in the same family.
explain: When you meet tuba, read the words around it. Biggest and lowest are clues that it is a large, deep-sounding instrument. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it.
fact: A tuba is a very large brass musical instrument with a wide bell.
fact: The tuba makes the lowest notes in a brass band or orchestra.
fact: In marching bands, the tuba often plays the "oom-pah" bass notes.
fact: Tuba is a noun: a tuba, two tubas. A person who plays one is a tuba player.
fact: You can say play the tuba, and the size of the player does not matter.
exercise: What kind of instrument is a tuba? | A drum that you hit with sticks | A small, high string instrument | A flute that you blow across the top | *A very large brass instrument with a wide bell
exercise: In a brass band, which instrument makes the lowest notes? | The trumpet | *The tuba | The flute | The triangle
exercise: Which word in «the trumpet is small and high» is the opposite of biggest? | trumpet | *small | high | the
test: In «The tuba is the biggest and lowest brass instrument», what does lowest mean? | Played only in the morning | The highest and loudest notes | *The deepest notes | Made of wood
test: Which of these is NOT in the brass family, according to «the trumpet, trombone, horn and tuba are brass»? | Tuba | Trumpet | *Clarinet | Horn
exam: Ella says a tuba is a small, high instrument. What is wrong with her idea? | A tuba is played by hitting it | A tuba has strings like a guitar | She is right, tubas are small | *A tuba is big and makes low notes
